# Review ownership. GitHub reads the last matching pattern.
#
# `@nonagenticai/maintainers` is the owner of record: the team exists, and the repository owner is
# a maintainer of it. GitHub requests the team's review on any pull request that touches an owned
# path. The `main` ruleset keeps `require_code_owner_review: false`: arming it while `*` is owned
# would require a team approval on every pull request (a blanket gate), while the owner decision
# (#93) is a code-owner review on the sensitive paths only — remove `*` first if it is armed.
* @nonagenticai/maintainers

# Sensitive paths: the CI definitions and the review policy itself. A change here needs a
# code-owner approval in addition to the required checks once the ruleset requires it; GitHub
# requests the team's review now.
/.github/workflows/** @nonagenticai/maintainers
/.github/CODEOWNERS @nonagenticai/maintainers
/SECURITY.md @nonagenticai/maintainers
/scripts/ci/** @nonagenticai/maintainers
